# motion-engine.pin - the hub's copy of the panel's door motion engine, by commit AND hash.
#
# Implements: SR-128, LLR-1357
#
# motion_engine.py beside this file is OfficeWallNaglight doorstream/motion.py at
# COMMIT with every comment removed and two docstrings (the module's and
# MotionEngine's) rewritten in neutral terms: this repository is public, and the
# source's comments record dated observations of a household (the Owner's ruling,
# 2026-10-27). The CODE is the panel's: the replay-validated detector the panel
# runs (WSN-023, WSN-106, WSN-107), so one detector, not two, decides what is
# motion at the door (HomeHub open-items A78: "pin it, don't fork it").
#
# Two checks hold that:
#   * camera_motion.py refuses to start when the file's sha256 is not SHA256 below
#     (the scrubbed file is what is pinned);
#   * tests/test_camera_motion.py TC-1543 compares the abstract syntax tree of this
#     file with `git show COMMIT:PATH` from the sibling OfficeWallNaglight checkout,
#     docstrings set aside: any change to the logic fails it.
#
# The file carries NO zones: its defaults are the whole image and no road band,
# which MotionConfig.eligible refuses. The real polygons are private (HomeHub
# scripts/deploy/config.homehub.psd1, T1) and reach the hub only in its .env.
#
# TO MOVE IT: take doorstream/motion.py from CameraOpt at a commit, scrub it the
# same way (comments out, the two docstrings neutral, no dates and no household
# detail), run TC-1543 against the new COMMIT, update COMMIT, LAST_CHANGE, SHA256
# and PINNED together, run a `camera_motion.py replay` over recorded segments, and
# commit them in one change.

SOURCE_REPO=OfficeWallNaglight
BRANCH=CameraOpt
COMMIT=b6310d1eed5dfece312b12a1d2831d54409fbf06
PATH=doorstream/motion.py
LAST_CHANGE=182f0f6483585a83782eeaad3ff5b233ebc454d9
SHA256=e5805b18a8a1eab8a0f3f09fc010f0357d24e3ebc714d92ce7142c7ac5b7bde5
SCRUBBED=comments removed; module and MotionEngine docstrings rewritten
PINNED=2026-10-27
